  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 528 PM MDT Sun Jul 26 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nPersistent upper level ridging, with axis off to the east, will keep \na southwesterly flow aloft in place across the Northern Rockies \nthrough this week. Hot daytime temperatures will continue this week, \npeaking late week and Saturday. A few weaker shortwaves progressing \nthrough the southwesterly flow aloft will foster some afternoon and \nevening showers and thunderstorms at times through the week. That \nsaid, this activity looks to be rather isolated most days. Gusty \nwinds would be the primary concern from a stronger thunderstorm that \ndevelops. \n\nConfidence is increasing in a ridge breakdown this weekend, which \nwould result in a breezy stretch over the plains and adjacent areas. \nAlthough some troughing looks to move through over this timeframe, \nconfidence in any precipitation remains low. -AM\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nForecast high temperatures this week:\n\nWildfire smoke will look to put a damper on forecast high \ntemperatures at times this week. Where confidence was high in ample \nsmoke, either aloft or at the surface, temperatures for Monday were \nadjusted cooler. Trends will continue to be monitored for additional \nadjustments to forecast high temperatures. -AM",
